  "kind": "tool",
  "description": "Analyze Hayabusa timelines to extract indicators, stack activity, and build focused reports.",
  "about": "Takajo reads the CSV or JSONL timelines produced by Hayabusa rather than parsing event logs itself. Its commands extract credentials, scripts, hashes, domains and IP addresses; stack processes, logons, services and tasks; build focused timelines and process trees; and generate static or locally served HTML reports. Keeping that boundary explicit matters: run Hayabusa first to produce the timeline, then point Takajo at that result.",
